{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 13,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, my eye hath seen all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", my ear hath heard and understood it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ye know, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the same",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " do I know also: I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not inferior to you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely I would speak to the Almighty, and I desire to reason with God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forgers of lies, ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all physicians of no value.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O that ye would altogether hold your peace and it would be your wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear now my reasoning, and hearken to the pleadings of my lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will ye speak wickedly for God? and talk deceitfully for him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will ye accept his person? will ye contend for God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is it good that he should search you out? or as one man mocketh another, do ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mock him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will surely reprove you, if ye do secretly accept persons.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall not his excellence make you afraid? and his dread fall upon you?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Your remembrances ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like to ashes, your bodies to bodies of clay.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hold your peace, let me alone, that I may speak, and let come on me what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why do I take my flesh in my teeth, and put my life in my hand?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though he shall slay me, yet will I trust in him: but I will maintain my own ways before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my salvation: for a hypocrite shall not come before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear diligently my speech, and my declaration with your ears.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold now, I have ordered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cause; I know that I shall be justified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will plead with me? for now, if I hold my tongue, I shall expire.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Only do not two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to me: then will I not hide myself from thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Withdraw thy hand far from me: and let not thy dread make me afraid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then call thou, and I will answer: or let me speak, and answer thou me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How many ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my iniquities and sins? make me to know my transgression and my sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why hidest thou thy face, and holdest me for thy enemy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou break a leaf driven to and fro? and wilt thou pursue the dry stubble?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou writest bitter things against me, and makest me to possess the iniquities of my youth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou puttest my feet also in the stocks, and lookest narrowly to all my paths; thou settest a print upon the heels of my feet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.13.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.13.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he, as a rotten thing, consumeth, as a garment that is moth-eaten.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
